QMacStyle: Size line edits and spin boxes like NSTextField under Liquid Glass

Not upstream: QMacStyle in dev, 6.11 and 6.10 (checked in November 2026)
has no Liquid Glass heights for line edits and spin boxes.

With Liquid Glass a bezeled NSTextField is 24, 22 and 19 pt tall for the
regular, small and mini control sizes. QMacStyle keeps a line edit at
21, 18 and 18 pt, the heights of the old design, and a spin box draws
its edit field 1 pt inside its frame at the top and the bottom, so its
bezel is only 19, 16 and 16 pt tall. A line edit or a spin box with a
frame now gets at least the height of the NSTextField of its control
size, and the edit field of a spin box takes its whole height, so both
are as tall as an AppKit text field next to them. The text stays
vertically centered, which puts it where AppKit has it, within half a
point. Frameless line edits, like the ones inside spin boxes and
editable combo boxes, are left as they are. Only Liquid Glass is
affected.

--- a/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
+++ b/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
@@ -362,6 +362,12 @@
     26, 22, 15
 };
 
+// Heights of a bezeled NSTextField with Liquid Glass, one for each of
+// QStyleHelper::WidgetSizePolicy. The text stays vertically centered.
+static const int textFieldLiquidGlassHeight[3] = {
+    24, 22, 19
+};
+
 static const int toolButtonArrowSize = 7;
